From b5b374929fbb969760f7c1b63ac937e6e9447401 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timon <timon2201@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 20:51:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] One package: drop the battery profile, merge performance into
 it

lunar-settings 2.0.0 is a single package again: common/ and performance/
are merged into files/, battery/ is gone. It replaces
lunar-tuning-performance and lunar-tuning-battery.

- sysctl (70-lunar.conf) and tmpfiles (lunar-thp.conf) set to the new
  lists; vm.defrag_soft and kernel.unprivileged_userns_clone are marked
  "-" so kernels without them (linux-lts) don't log errors
- kernel parameters in one file, 10-lunar.conf, with
  intel_idle.max_cstate=1 added (processor.max_cstate only affects
  acpi_idle, which Intel CPUs don't use)
- lunar-amdgpu-performance and the performance power profile are enabled
  by lunar-settings.install

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NRvVgxhmC2rjcLktTFXtAX
